This is the assert statement that's corresponding to the comments in the provided C# code. The & operator is used to express logical AND operation. In the C# code, this assert statement checks the condition that if the calculated return value is non-negative (New_Ret >= 0) and new array list's last index of x is less than or equal to old array list's count (New_arrListLastIndexOfX <= Old_arrListCount). If the condition is true, this portion of code will simply continue executing. If the condition is false, the debugger will stop program execution and throw an exception. 

For additional code understanding, you should consider C# language syntax specifics. The provided statement relates to debugging purposes, so using it in production might be against best practices. 

Debug.Assert usage is typically used for assertions within your code to verify its invariants and states. But please use them thoughtfully as they can significantly degrade performance especially in production code.--------------------
