In the second example, there is only one comment related to assert statement, so the output would be:
```cs
Debug.Assert(Old_arrListLastIndexOfX == New_arrListLastIndexOfX);
```
This checks if the last index of `x` is equal to the count of old array before `IndexOf(x)` is called. If it is equal and the new return value is non negative, it means `IndexOf(x)` did not change the index of `x` and indeed, it is valid that last index of 'x' in the new array is less or equal to the count of old array.--------------------